 the tightness in your  jaw and the you know the angle of your  uh of your body language like  that i thought would read it's like oh  all of that gets lost so i have to just  be thinking about  like eyes nose lips that's it because  i thought i was like you know conveying  uh my uh my emotions and what's at stake  and everything like through  my performance and then you realize like  oh so little of it is on screen and you  forget like how much you rely on  uh your body language and you know your  neck and your jaw and stuff and  yeah to just be limited to this much of  your face was  challenging thankfully we had great  stunt people who helped us out as well  and the the final footage was  so much more sophisticated than what i  thought it was going to be based on what  i was trying to do  you know in those scenes because you  know we were focused on  just trying to climb properly and and  not fall down  yeah it's definitely a nail-biting  sequence on that note i gotta go  just gonna say congrats hope you guys  stay safe and uh be well  thank you

